# Project template

Part of the [[README]]. Skeleton for a new Project in `Projects/`. Rules: [[gtd]], [[schema]], [[body-sections]].

**Using it:** [[= owner =]] creates a new file in `Projects/`, and Templater fills it. Agents copy it by hand and save it as `Projects/<slug>.md`. Both, in detail: [[template-task]]. Then:

- Add `area:` (a list, at least one) — required.
- Replace the first body line with the outcome: what "done" looks like.
- Create the first next action as a task with `project` pointing here, in the same change. A `not-started` project has at least one; queue later steps as `queued` tasks.
- Use `phase: planned` instead if the project starts later; say when in the body.
- Optional fields: [[schema]] (`due` only for hard deadlines).

<%*
tR = "";
let title = tp.file.title;
if (title.startsWith("Untitled")) title = await tp.system.prompt("Project title (sentence case, names the outcome)");
const slug = title.normalize("NFKD").replace(/[^\x00-\x7F]/g, "").toLowerCase().replace(/'/g, "").replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, "-").replace(/^-+|-+$/g, "");
await tp.file.move("Projects/" + slug);
-%>
